    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.6, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"Q1\", \"L1\", \"R1\"], \"pins\": [\"Q1.3\", \"L1.1\"], \"nets\": [\"GND\", \"Display_Power_Switch\"], \"observed\": \"Q1 drain (pin 3) and one terminal of boost inductor L1 (pin 1) are both on the GND net. L1 pin 2 sits on Display_Power_Switch, which is fed from the Q2 drain. Q1's source returns through R1 to GND, so the MOSFET has both drain and source on ground and cannot switch the inductor node.\", \"expected\": \"The boost inductor should run from the switched input rail (Display_Power_Switch) to the Q1 drain/SW node, with Q1 source going through the 0.47 \u03a9 sense resistor R1 to GND. Q1 drain must not be tied to GND, and the inductor must not be returned directly to GND.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"L1\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\" }, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"Q1\\\") (pin \\\"3\\\") (pinfunction \\\"D\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"L1 0 Display_Power_Switch 10u\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Q1 \u2014 EPD boost-converter switch; R1 0.47 \u03a9 current-sense resistor (EPD booster current-limit sense)\"}], \"impact\": \"The boost converter cannot generate the panel's high-voltage rails. Q1 is short-circuited across its drain-source, so the inductor is clamped to ground and the EPD driver will not work correctly.\", \"confidence\": 0.6}, {\"category\": \"footprint_mismatch\", \"components\": [\"C11\"], \"pins\": [\"C11.1\", \"C11.2\"], \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\", \"GND\"], \"observed\": \"C11 is a 0.1uF Device:C capacitor, but its footprint is an inductor land pattern (Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder). Pin 1 is on its own unconnected net and only pin 2 reaches GND, so it does nothing as a decoupling cap.\", \"expected\": \"A decoupling capacitor should have a capacitor footprint with both pins connected, bridging a supply and ground.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"58\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"}], \"impact\": \"The capacitor is electrically inert, so it adds no decoupling or filtering. If it was meant to sit on a supply, that supply is left without the intended bypass.\", \"confidence\": 0.35}]], \"summary\": \"The EPD boost stage has Q1's drain and one end of L1 both on GND, which shorts the switching node and defeats the boost converter. Capacitor C11 also has a floating pin and an inductor footprint, which points to a second, lower-confidence wiring/footprint fault.\"}",
